.TH "libnvmf_read_key" 9 "libnvmf_read_key" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_read_key \- Read key raw data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_read_key
.BI "(struct libnvme_global_ctx *ctx "  ","
.BI "long keyring_id "  ","
.BI "long key_id "  ","
.BI "int *len "  ","
.BI "unsigned char **key "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "ctx" 12
struct libnvme_global_ctx object
.IP "keyring_id" 12
Id of the keyring holding \fIkey_id\fP
.IP "key_id" 12
Key id
.IP "len" 12
Length of \fIkey\fP to return
.IP "key" 12
Raw key data to return
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Links the keyring specified by \fIkeyring_id\fP into the session
keyring and reads the payload of the key specified by \fIkey_id\fP.
\fIlen\fP holds the size of the returned buffer.
If \fIkeyring_id\fP is 0 the default keyring '.nvme' is used.
.SH "RETURN"
0 on success, negative error code otherwise.
